assistant
<think> Alright, so I have this problem here about line segments and their perpendicular bisectors, and I need to find the area of a region R, which consists of all midpoints P of segments XY where X is on AB and Y is on CD. Let me try to parse this step by step.

First, let me restate the problem in my own words to make sure I understand it. We have a line segment AB with a perpendicular bisector CD. Importantly, C is given as the midpoint of AB. Wait a second, hold on—that seems contradictory, doesn’t it?

